  "title": "113: Al-Falaq الفلق",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "This is a ‘Madani’ Surah and it has 5 verses. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that whoever recites this Surah in the month of Ramazan in any of his prayers, it is as if he has fasted in Makkah and he will get the reward for performing Hajj and Umrah.\nImam Muhammad al-Baqir (a.s.) said that in the prayer of Shafa’a (in Salaatul-layl) one should recite Surah al-Falaq in the first rak’aat and an-Naas in the second.\nبِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nقُلْ اَعُوْذُ بِرَبِّ الْفَلَقِۙ‏(1)\nQUL A-OO’ZO BE RABBIL FALAQ. \nSay: I seek refuge in the Lord of the dawn, \nمِنْ شَرِّ مَا خَلَقَۙ‏(2)\nMIN SHARRE MAA KHALAQ. \nFrom the evil of what He has created, \nوَمِنْ شَرِّ غَاسِقٍ اِذَا وَقَبَۙ‏(3)\nWA MIN SHARRE GHAASEQIN EZAA WAQAB. \nAnd from the evil of the utterly dark night when it comes, \nوَمِنْ شَرِّ النَّفّٰثٰتِ فِى الْعُقَدِۙ‏(4)\nWA MIN SHARRIN NAFFAASAATE FIL O’QADE. \nAnd from the evil of those who blow on knots, \nوَمِنْ شَرِّ حَاسِدٍ اِذَا حَسَدَ‏(5)\nWA MIN SHARRE HAASEDIN EZAA HASAD.\nAnd from the evil of the envious when he envies "
